 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bekhorot.43b.13",
   "daf": "43b",
   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ אֵין לוֹ גְּבִינִין, אוֹ אֵין לוֹ אֶלָּא גְּבִין אֶחָד — זֶהוּ גִּבֵּן הָאָמוּר בְּתוֹרָה. רַבִּי דּוֹסָא אוֹמֵר: (שֶׁגְּבִינִין) [שֶׁגְּבִינָיו] שׁוֹכְבִין. רַבִּי חֲנִינָא בֶּן אַנְטִיגְנוֹס אוֹמֵר: שֶׁיֵּשׁ לוֹ שְׁנֵי גַּבִּין וּשְׁתֵּי שִׁדְרָאוֹת.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» If a priest «has no eyebrows, or» if «he has only one eyebrow, that is the gibben that is stated in the Torah» in the list of blemished priests (see Leviticus 21:20). «Rabbi Dosa says:» A gibben is one «whose eyebrows» are so long that they «lie» flat and cover his eyes. «Rabbi Ḥanina ben Antigonus says:» A gibben is one «who has two backs and two spines.»"
  }
 ],
